-- title:
--   Per-node block for traces of ends on K₀ at q=3
-- statement:
--   The setting is the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-style rigid level at the small prime $q$, with a guard prime dividing the tame part of the level.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** $q$ is a prime with $q=3$; $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$ (`hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`); $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\neq q$, $\ell\nmid M'$ (`hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`).
--
--   **Local base.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non‑unit of $A$ (`hA`, i.e. `A.LiesOverPrime q`); $k_0$ is a subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ containing $\mathbb Q$, and $A_0:=$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` is the induced valuation subring $A\cap k_0$ of $k_0$; $\pi_0\in k_0$ lies in $A$ (`hπ`). The *local hypotheses* are: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), henselian (`hhens`), with algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$ (`hκ`); and $\ell_g-1$ is a unit of $A_0$ (`htame`, tameness of the guard level).
--
--   **Uniformisers and roots of unity.** $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$‑th root of unity (`hζ₀`) and $\xi\in k_0$ a primitive $q$‑th root of unity (`hξ`); $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ (`hϖtA`) and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`); $\varpi_t'\in A_0$ has image $\varpi_t$ (`hϖt'`); $m\ge 1$ satisfies $\pi_0^m=\varpi_t'\cdot w$ with $w$ a unit of $A_0$ (`hm1`, `hm`). Further frame data: $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b=\bot$ (`hKb`), $A_b$ a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$ (`hAb`), with maximal ideal generated by $\varpi_b\neq 0$ (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`).
--
--   **Modular data.** $H_1=$ `levelH q M'` $\cap\ \ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times\big)$ (`hH₁`), where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction of unit groups attached to `dvd_sq_mul q M'`; $K_\ell$ is the base change to $k_0$ of the function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$, i.e. $K_\ell=$ `laurentBaseChange k₀ (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)` (`hKℓ`), an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq k_0((\mathsf q))$; $j_\ell\in K_\ell$ is nonzero with Laurent series the coefficientwise image of the $j$‑expansion `jq` (`hjℓ`), and `jqNModC k₀ q` lies in $K_\ell$ (`hjK`). Places of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$, of the reduced function fields, etc. are valuation subrings containing the base field, proper and principal, as in `Place`.
--
--   **Reduction data.** $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` with $W$ exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` (`hW`): rational, affine geometric places $w$ whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator $j$ is a supersingular $j$‑invariant, meaning every elliptic curve with that $j$ has no nonzero $q$‑torsion point; $s\in W$ is one of them. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` along $A$ from $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F(M')=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` with a surjective residue map onto the reduced field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$, together with a degree‑preserving map on places); `hle` records `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`, and `hR₀` says that the residue map of $R_0$ is coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series along $A\to\operatorname{ResidueField} A$.
--
--   **The supersingular point.** $y$ is a maximal ideal (`hy`) of the chart algebra `chartAlgFin A₀ Kℓ jℓ`, the subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$, with $\pi_0\in y$ (`hϖy`); `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, $\varphi(j_\ell)$ is supersingular. The *moduli dictionary* `hover` states: for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `R₀.integers`, which has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which `jq` has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$‑residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the chart element `coeffEmb k₀ g` satisfies: for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue in $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, the difference of `coeffEmb k₀ g` and $c$ lies in $y$. The *orbit* hypothesis `hOrbit` states that any maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying the same dictionary is obtained from $y$ by a level automorphism: there are $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ an automorphism of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` — the condition that on quotients of modular forms of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$‑expansions, the $q$‑expansion of $\tau x$ matches the slash action by `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`, under any embedding $k_0\to\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$ — such that $\tau$ preserves the chart algebra and transports $y$ to $y'$.
--
--   **The rigid model over $K_\ell$.** $B_t$ is an $A_0$‑subalgebra of $K_\ell$ and $W_t$ a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with $B_t\subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hS1` is a fourteen‑fold conjunction, summarised here: the chart algebra is contained in $B_t$ and $K_\ell$ is its fraction field; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$ with special fibre of Krull dimension at most $1$; $W_t$ is a discrete valuation ring with constants $A_0$, uniformiser $\pi_0$, cutting out $y$ on the chart algebra, and is the localisation of $B_t$ at its maximal ideal; for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$‑algebra structure on the residue field of $A_0$ there is a surjection of $B_t$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) over that residue field with kernel given by the maximal ideal of $W_t$, compatible with constants, equivariant for level automorphisms via `redQ` and `hAction` on `hSubgroup`, with a non‑triviality clause for $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and a clause producing a level automorphism realising the scalar $c$ with trivial matrix part; $B_t$ is stable under level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is a level translate of the one cut out by $W_t$; and $\pi_0$ divides any element of $B_t$ vanishing at all such translates.
--
--   **Monodromy and ends.** $n\ge1$ divides $q+1$ (`hn1`, `hnq`) and equals $2\cdot$`placeWidthChar q M' s` (`hn`), the latter being `jWidthChar q` of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(j)$ divided by the $j$‑ramification of $s$ (at $q=3$, `jWidthChar` is $6$ at $j=0$ and $1$ otherwise); $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hγ₀Γ`, `hγ₀Γ0`) and $\tau_0$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ (`hτ₀`) preserving $W_t$ (`hτ₀W`); $\zeta_c$ in the $\mathfrak m$‑adic completion $\widehat A_0$ satisfies $\zeta_c^n=1$ and $\zeta_c^k-1$ is a unit for $0<k<n$ (`hζc`, `hζcprim`). Moreover `jqNModC k₀ q` lies in the chart algebra (`hjC`) and its difference with $a_0\in A_0$ lies in $y$ (`ha₀y`). `ends` is a finite set of subrings of $K_\ell$, and `hR7` is a twelve‑fold conjunction, summarised here: $\tau_0$ acts on $B_t$ with exact order $n$ and every $W_t$‑preserving level automorphism agrees on $B_t$ with a power $\tau_0^k$, $k<n$; `ends` has $q+1$ elements, is permuted by the $W_t$‑preserving level automorphisms for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, transitively so, each end being $\tau_0$‑stable, and distinct ends are separated by an element which is a non‑unit in one and a unit in the other; there is a finite‑type, level‑stable subalgebra $B_c$ contained in every end, each end being a localisation of $B_c$; a level automorphism mapping an end into $W_t$ preserves $W_t$; each end is a local noetherian subring of $W_t$ containing the chart algebra, with constants $A_0$ and residue field generated by constants, whose completion is identified by some $\iota$ with $\widehat A_0[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^m)$ so that constants are constants, $c_x\mapsto \gamma_U U$, $c_y\mapsto \gamma_V V$, $c_xc_y=\pi_0^m u$, the image of `jqNModC k₀ q` $-\,a_0$ is $w_V V^{\,e}$ with $e\ge1$, $\tau_0$ corresponds to an automorphism $\theta_0$ with $\theta_0U\equiv\zeta_cU$ and $\theta_0V\equiv\zeta_c^{-1}V$ modulo the square of the maximal ideal, together with an Igusa branch $W_x$ (a discrete valuation ring over $A_0$ with uniformiser $\pi_0$, a residually transcendental parameter, $c_x$ in and $c_y$ out of its maximal ideal, cutting out $y$ on the chart, separating this end from the others) and a node chart $B_x$ (level‑stable, finite type, regular where $j_\ell$ is, presenting the end as a localisation, and containing an element with a pole at every valuation subring at which $j_\ell$ is residually transcendental and which fails to contain the end); finally, any valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with constants $A_0$ containing the chart algebra and centred at $y$ either contains $B_t$ or dominates one of the ends.
--
--   **Two further pole hypotheses.** `hR9`: some $b\in B_t$ lies outside every valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ with constants $A_0$, with $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, and at which $j_\ell$ is residually transcendental (no monic $A_0$‑integral polynomial in $j_\ell$ lies in the maximal ideal). `hR10`: for every maximal ideal $y''$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ which is not a level translate of $y$, some $b\in B_t$ lies outside every valuation subring containing the chart algebra and centred at the corresponding translate of $y''$, for all level automorphisms with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   **Descent data.** $G$ is the subgroup of $\operatorname{Aut}(K_\ell/k_0)$ generated by all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`); $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`); $B_0$ consists of the $G$‑invariant elements of $B_t$ (`hB₀`); $W_0'$ is the valuation subring of $K_0$ whose elements are those lying in $W_t$ (`hW₀'`); `nodes` is a finite set of subrings of $K_0$, each of which is the trace on $K_0$ of some end (`hnodes`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every end $\tilde{\mathcal O}\in$ `ends` and every subring $\mathcal O$ of $K_0$ equal to the preimage of $\tilde{\mathcal O}$ under $K_0\hookrightarrow K_\ell$, all of the following hold.
--
--   (1) $\mathcal O\subseteq W_0'$, and there are a local ring structure and a noetherian ring structure on $\mathcal O$ such that: for $x\in k_0$ one has $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $K_0$ lies in $\mathcal O$; and for every $f\in\mathcal O$ there is $x\in k_0$ with $x\in A$ and image in $\mathcal O$ such that $f-x$ is not a unit of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   (2) There exist $E_0\ge1$; an element $v\in k_0$ with $v\in A$ and $v^{-1}\in A$ such that $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,2\cdot\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s}\cdot v$; a proof that $\pi_0$ lies in $\mathcal O$; elements $c_x,c_y\in\mathcal O$; a unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$; a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the completion of $\mathcal O$ at its maximal ideal onto $\widehat A_0[[U,V]]/(UV-\hat\pi_0^{\,E_0})$, where $\widehat A_0$ is the completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal and the crossing model is `UVCrossingModel`; and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that crossing model, such that:
--
--   (2a) $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $\mathcal O$;
--
--   (2b) for every $x\in k_0$ with $x\in A$ and image in $\mathcal O$, $\iota$ sends the image of $x$ in the completion to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $x$ in $\widehat A_0$;
--
--   (2c) $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$;
--
--   (2d) $c_y\in W_0'$ and $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0'$, while $c_x$, whenever it lies in $W_0'$, lies outside the maximal ideal of $W_0'$;
--
--   (2e) the element `jqNModC k₀ q` $-\,a_0$ of $K_\ell$ lies in $K_0$ and in $\mathcal O$, and there are $e\ge1$ and a unit $w_V$ of the crossing model with $\iota$ of it equal to $w_V\cdot V^{\,e}$;
--
--   (2f) there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_0$ such that: $\mathcal O\subseteq W_x$; for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $W_x$; $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring; $\pi_0$ lies in $W_x$ and generates its maximal ideal; there is $t\in W_x$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in $W_x$ and in its maximal ideal; $c_x$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ does not; and the moduli dictionary holds on $W_x$: for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change lies in `R₀.integers` and which has non-negative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which `jq` has non-negative order, and with `coeffEmb k₀ g` $\in K_\ell$, that element lies in $K_0$ and in $W_x$, it lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if its $R_0$‑residue is zero, and if its $R_0$‑residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$ then the element lies in $\mathcal O$ and, for every $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$ and image in $\mathcal O$ whose residue in $\operatorname{ResidueField} A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$‑residue, the difference of the element and $c$ is not a unit of $\mathcal O$; finally, for every $\mathcal O'\in$ `nodes` with $\mathcal O'\neq\mathcal O$ there is $f\in\mathcal O'$ with $f\notin W_x$;
--
--   (2g) there is a subring $B_x$ of $K_0$ such that: every $f\in B_x$ has image in $B_0$ and lies in $\mathcal O$; every $f\in B_x$ satisfies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ for every place $P$ of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$ with $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(j_\ell)$; $\mathcal O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ along its units, that is $f\in\mathcal O$ if and only if $f\cdot h=g$ for some $g,h\in B_x$ with $h$ a unit of $\mathcal O$ whenever $h\in\mathcal O$; $K_0$ is the field of fractions of $B_x$ (for every $f\in K_0$ there are $g,h\in B_x$ with $h\neq0$ and $fh=g$); there is a finite set $T\subseteq K_0$ with $B_x$ the subring generated by the images of the elements of $k_0$ lying in $A$ together with $T$; and there is $b\in B_x$ such that for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with the properties that for $x\in k_0$ one has $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $V$, that $\pi_0$ lies in the maximal ideal of $V$, and that, for the element `coeffEmb k₀ jq` of $K_\ell$ lying in $K_0$ and in $V$, no monic polynomial over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$ evaluated at it lies in the maximal ideal of $V$, the existence of some $f\in\mathcal O$ with $f\notin V$ forces $b\notin V$.
--
--   This is the per‑node step in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ at the small prime $q=3$: it transports the crossing‑model presentation, the Igusa branch and the node chart from an end of the rigid model over $K_\ell$ to its trace on the descended field $K_0=K_\ell^G$, and records that the traced node is local, noetherian, with constants $A\cap k_0$, with completion $\widehat A_0[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$ and with the correct moduli dictionary at the supersingular place $s$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_fixedField_of_rigidChart_ends_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_fixedField_of_rigidChart_ends_of_eq_three_of_dvd), which assembles the descended nodes into the special fibre.
